From 82fb94a7ff4f03f7e3763c62c59ae812571bc9cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tesseract XRT port <jwkim@limagin.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:10:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 02/19] xocl/xiic: build without I2C_CLASS_SPD (Linux 6.10)

Mainline commit e61bcf42d290 ("i2c: Remove I2C_CLASS_SPD", v6.10)
deleted the I2C_CLASS_SPD adapter class bit after commit 9fd12f385720
(v6.8) had removed the last client driver that matched on it. xiic.c
still sets it on its adapter, which no longer compiles.

Guard: feature test "#ifdef I2C_CLASS_SPD" (it is a plain macro in
<linux/i2c.h>), so the original initializer is kept on every kernel
that still defines the bit, including 6.8 and 6.9.

Equivalence: where the macro exists nothing changes. Where it does not,
no i2c driver can match on class bit 7 any more, so the adapter offers
exactly the same probing behaviour with I2C_CLASS_HWMON alone.

Upstream: XRT commit 04350f685 makes the same change but switches at
KERNEL_VERSION(6, 8, 0), which drops the bit on 6.8/6.9 where it still
exists; this patch keeps it there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SpY5QiU1d7kAe8YJM35EvA
---
 driver/xocl/subdev/xiic.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/driver/xocl/subdev/xiic.c b/driver/xocl/subdev/xiic.c
index 39499c6..f0d0658 100644
--- a/driver/xocl/subdev/xiic.c
+++ b/driver/xocl/subdev/xiic.c
@@ -861,7 +861,12 @@ static const struct i2c_algorithm xiic_algorithm = {
 
 static struct i2c_adapter xiic_adapter = {
 	.owner = THIS_MODULE,
+#ifdef I2C_CLASS_SPD
 	.class = I2C_CLASS_HWMON | I2C_CLASS_SPD,
+#else
+	/* I2C_CLASS_SPD was removed in Linux 6.10 (commit e61bcf42d290) */
+	.class = I2C_CLASS_HWMON,
+#endif
 	.algo = &xiic_algorithm,
 };
 
